  displayName: Atlantic cod
  scientificName: Gadus morhua
  description: A large cold-water fish of the North Atlantic, recognized by its streamlined
    body and distinctive chin barbel. Atlantic cod are important predators in temperate
    marine ecosystems and often inhabit rocky reefs and kelp-covered coastlines.
  depthLayer: 
  behavior: Moves slowly through the midwater and near the seafloor, investigating
    rocky structures and kelp stands. May pause in place before making short bursts
    to pursue prey.
